WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Welcome to our 30-minute overview of selling in the Amazon Store.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.800
Every Amazon seller has a few things in common.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.100
To get started, they create a selling account.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.000
Then they list products, fulfill customer orders, and receive payment.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.700
To maintain good account health, sellers should also monitor their customer service performance,

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.700
Amazon policy compliance, and shipping performance.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.700
Sellers can take advantage of a range of Amazon tools and programs too.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:37.811
They can enroll eligible brands in Amazon brand registry to enjoy access to additional selling benefits

00:00:37.811 --> 00:00:38.700
and protections.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:44.700
They can use fulfillment by Amazon or FBA to help deliver items to customers.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.811
They can also use deals and coupons to promote products and sponsored campaigns and other Amazon

00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:52.700
ads services

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.700
to feature items in the Amazon Store.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.700
When sellers want to understand their sales better,

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.700
they can use Amazon-provided dashboards, reports, and data

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.700
along with tools that let them adjust their selling strategies.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:12.700
To get you started on your selling journey, let's review some of the basic steps for selling in

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.700
the Amazon Store

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.700
and explore common tools and programs.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.700
The first thing you need to start selling in the Amazon Store is a selling account.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.900
If you don't have one already, visit sell.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:25.300
amazon.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:25.700
com.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.700
Click the Sign Up button and then click the Create Your Amazon Account button.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:36.242
On the next page, enter your first and last name along with the email address and password you want

00:01:36.242 --> 00:01:37.700
to access your account with.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.700
Click the Next button, then check your email for a one-time password.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:49.557
Enter that password where it says Verify Email Address, then click the Create Your Amazon Account

00:01:49.557 --> 00:01:51.700
button to continue account registration.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:58.064
During registration, you'll provide information about you and your business along with details we

00:01:58.064 --> 00:02:01.700
use to set up payment and settlement processing.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:07.595
You can use our list of frequently asked questions throughout registration to get help with specific

00:02:07.595 --> 00:02:08.700
selections and entries.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:15.759
When selecting your business type, make sure you pick the correct classification as it determines

00:02:15.759 --> 00:02:16.700
subsequent entries.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:23.367
And if you enter a business name, make sure it's the name used to register with your state or federal

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:23.700
government.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:28.700
That should be the exact name that appears on your business registration document.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:38.075
Before clicking the Agree and Continue button, review relevant policies and notices using the links

00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:38.700
provided.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.700
Next, on the Business Information page, enter a company registration number if applicable, as well

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.700
as the address for your business.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:50.700
Your business address should be the address your business is registered under, or your operating

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.700
address if you're an individual entity.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:59.700
Next, enter a phone number, then click the button below to receive a one-time PIN via your phone.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.700
Enter that PIN in the pop-up after you receive it and click the Verify button.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:12.367
Complete the Business Information portion of seller registration by entering the name of your business's

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:13.700
primary contact person.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:20.245
Make sure this name matches that person's entire name as it appears on a government-issued ID, like

00:03:20.245 --> 00:03:21.700
a license or passport.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:28.557
Then, click the Next button to proceed to the Seller Information page, where you'll enter personal

00:03:28.557 --> 00:03:30.700
information for your primary contact.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.700
Select a country of citizenship, country of birth, and birth date.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.700
Then, provide a residential address and mobile phone number.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:44.795
You'll also need to select whether your primary contact is a beneficial owner of your business,

00:03:44.795 --> 00:03:46.700
a legal representative, or both.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:52.700
Make sure you add other beneficial owners if your business has more than one.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:58.109
Click the Save button to proceed to the billing page, where you'll enter bank account and credit

00:03:58.109 --> 00:03:59.700
card information for your business.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:05.700
Your bank account information is used to transfer your sales proceeds on a regular cycle.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:12.233
Current credit card information is required for all sellers and prevents settlement and listing

00:04:12.233 --> 00:04:12.700
issues.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:18.700
When you've completed your billing information, you'll be prompted to provide the necessary store

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.700
and identity verification information for your business.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:27.347
That completes the registration process, which means you can sign in to your new Seller Central

00:04:27.347 --> 00:04:27.700
account.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.700
Seller Central is your hub for selling in the Amazon store.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.700
You can configure your Seller Central account using various settings.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:43.986
You'll use the selections in the main menu to navigate to tools for listing products, managing inventory,

00:04:43.986 --> 00:04:45.700
and fulfilling customer orders.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:52.557
The main menu is also how you find advertising services, payment and business reports, the Account

00:04:52.557 --> 00:04:57.700
Health Dashboard, and other tools for managing the performance of your business.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:02.700
It provides access to resources that can support the growth of your business, too.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:09.222
That includes our Growth Opportunities page, which offers a customized list of asin-level recommendations

00:05:09.222 --> 00:05:12.700
based on the sales potential of your products.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:19.382
If you're a professional seller, you'll see a section in the main menu for B2B or Business to Business

00:05:19.382 --> 00:05:19.700
features.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:26.238
And if you enrolled your brand in Amazon Brand Registry or are affiliated with an enrolled brand,

00:05:26.238 --> 00:05:29.700
you'll see a section that contains brand selling benefits.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:36.900
We also provide resources in Seller Central to answer questions and help you learn how to use tools

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:37.700
and programs.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:45.135
You can use the search bar at the top of the page to locate specific help pages, Seller University

00:05:45.135 --> 00:05:46.700
content, or Seller forums.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:51.700
If you ever need more support, click "Help" in the top right corner.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:57.700
Now that you're more familiar with Seller Central, let's review a few common selling processes starting

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.700
with enrolling a brand in Amazon Brand Registry.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:07.474
We'll also provide quick overviews of the listing process, competitive pricing, FBA, the Account

00:06:07.474 --> 00:06:15.216
Health Dashboard, and some of the tools Amazon sellers use to promote and advertise products and

00:06:15.216 --> 00:06:15.700
brands.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:19.700
We'll end with guidance for managing customer reviews and feedback.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:26.582
Although listing products is the step new sellers often think of first, if you're the owner of an

00:06:26.582 --> 00:06:32.700
eligible brand, we recommend you start your selling journey by enrolling it in Amazon Brand Registry.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:38.347
You'll want to do this before you list your products so they're associated with your registered

00:06:38.347 --> 00:06:38.700
brand.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:45.367
Brand Registry is a free program that provides eligible brands with access to additional selling

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:46.700
benefits and protections.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:53.900
After enrolling, brands can use tools like stores, A+ content, and sponsored brands, which can help

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:55.700
them reach more customers.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:02.450
They also enjoy greater control over their product detail pages and access to additional automated

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:04.700
protections, programs, and reporting options.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.700
To enroll your brand, you need to meet a few basic requirements.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:16.000
You need your brand name or a logo that includes your brand name permanently affixed to your products

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:16.700
or packaging.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:23.352
You also need an active registered trademark for your brand name or logo, or a pending trademark

00:07:23.352 --> 00:07:25.700
application or registration in some cases.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.911
If you meet these basic requirements, visit brandservices.

00:07:29.911 --> 00:07:30.437
amazon.

00:07:30.437 --> 00:07:35.700
com to review country-specific requirements and enroll your brand.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:42.450
If you don't meet these requirements, you may still be able to list your branded products in the

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:47.700
Amazon Store by requesting approval for an unregistered brand name during the listing process.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:53.347
You'll complete a selling application in this scenario, which we'll review a little later in this

00:07:53.347 --> 00:07:53.700
video.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:59.700
When you're ready to list a product in the Amazon Store, whether it's a branded product you own

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:05.367
or one you're reselling, you add the product to your Amazon inventory and make it available for

00:08:05.367 --> 00:08:05.700
sale.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:12.700
All active listed products are viewable to Amazon customers via a unique product detail page.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:20.700
That page includes a product title, at least one image, about this item bullets, and a product description.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:27.277
If the product you want to sell already exists in the Amazon Store, you'll list it by matching an

00:08:27.277 --> 00:08:29.700
offer to the existing product detail page.

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:36.900
If it's not already in the Amazon Store, you'll create a product detail page and add your offer

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:37.700
information simultaneously.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.700
Let's review the steps for matching a product first.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:44.700
Start by hovering over catalog in the main menu.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.613
Then click Add Products.

00:08:46.613 --> 00:08:55.700
On the next page, search for your product using a product ID like a UPC, ISBN, EAN, or JAN.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:01.700
These product IDs are all types of GTINs or Global Trade Item Numbers.

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:06.700
Each GTIN is paired with a unique barcode, which makes products scannable.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:11.048
Locate the product you want to sell in the results.

00:09:11.048 --> 00:09:16.700
When you find it, select the appropriate condition, new, used, or another type.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:22.700
If you see a sell this product button, click it to start entering your offer information.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:29.100
If you see an Apply to Sell button, click Show Limitations directly below to understand requirements

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.700
for listing the product.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:36.700
Then click the Apply to Sell button to complete one or more required selling applications.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:42.700
You may need to complete a selling application for a category, a brand, or both.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:49.700
After completing each application and receiving approval from Amazon, you can enter your offer information.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:55.460
You'll enter a variety of information on the offer page, including your standard price, which is

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.700
what customers see when they first see your offer.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:06.700
This price doesn't include any shipping fees, promotions, discounts, or other order related expenses.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:12.963
You can create and manage those using separate tools in Seller Central, and customers see them applied

00:10:12.963 --> 00:10:13.700
at checkout.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.700
The Offer page is also where you enter start and end dates for a sale.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:23.700
Select gift services you'd like to provide, and enter notes on your product's condition.

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:29.595
Near the bottom of the page, you'll select either yourself or Amazon as the fulfillment channel

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:30.700
for the product.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:37.700
We'll provide more information about both merchant fulfillment or MFN, and fulfillment by Amazon

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.700
or FBA later in this video.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:47.033
If you want to add a product that's not already in the Amazon store, we recommend starting the listing

00:10:47.033 --> 00:10:51.700
process the same way you would for a match by searching the Amazon catalog.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:56.700
This helps ensure the product is genuinely new and avoid duplicate listings.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:11:02.771
When you've confirmed your product isn't in the search results, click the Create a New Listing button

00:11:02.771 --> 00:11:06.700
to provide information for both your product detail page and offer.

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:10.700
Start by selecting your product type or category.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:15.700
You can search or browse by clicking a category, then one or more subcategories.

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:21.700
If you see a Learn More button with a lock, your category requires approval.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:27.700
Click the button to review our categories and products that require approval help page, and then

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:30.700
click the link to the appropriate selling application.

00:11:30.700 --> 00:11:36.700
We'll review your application, and if you're approved, you can continue the listing process.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:43.743
If you see a Select button while choosing a category for your product, click it to begin entering

00:11:43.743 --> 00:11:45.700
your product and offer information.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:49.700
You'll use four main sections to enter product information.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:57.700
In the Vital Info section, you'll enter key product information like ID number, brand, and manufacturer.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:12:03.597
Keep in mind that if you're trying to add a branded product to the Amazon catalog, the brand name

00:12:03.597 --> 00:12:06.700
you enter or select needs to be approved by Amazon.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:12.700
You'll either need to enroll your brand or complete a selling application in Seller Central.

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:18.839
If you need to complete a selling application for an unregistered brand, you'll be prompted to do

00:12:18.839 --> 00:12:25.339
so by error 5665, which will appear after you enter the unregistered brand name in the brand name

00:12:25.339 --> 00:12:25.700
field.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:31.820
In the Offer section, you'll enter and select the same kind of pricing, sales, and fulfillment information

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:34.700
that you'd enter for a product you're matching.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:40.700
In the Images section, you'll upload at least one image for your product detail page.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:47.100
We recommend reviewing our listing guidelines before doing so, and encourage you to review our product

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.700
image requirements help page by clicking the link provided.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:57.046
If your product is available in different versions for color, size, style, or other attributes,

00:12:57.046 --> 00:13:01.700
you'll use the Variations page to provide information for each version.

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:08.700
At Amazon, we group variations or child products on a single detail page for a parent product.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.700
That helps customers find and compare versions.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:18.892
If you have more product information to add, click the More Attributes toggle to display the tabs

00:13:18.892 --> 00:13:22.700
for the compliance, description, keywords, and more details sections.

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:28.322
When you've entered all required information in fields with red borders, as well as any optional

00:13:28.322 --> 00:13:34.295
information you want to include, click the Save and Finish button at the bottom of each section

00:13:34.295 --> 00:13:35.700
to submit your information.

00:13:35.700 --> 00:13:41.700
If your new product is approved, its detail page should appear within 24 hours.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:48.500
When you create or suggest updates to a product detail page, it's important to follow Amazon guidelines

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:53.700
and employ best practices to help customers find and engage with your product.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:14:00.500
Before you create your first product detail page, search Seller Central for our product page style

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:00.925
guide.

00:14:00.925 --> 00:14:06.875
This includes links to downloadable style guides for each product category, full requirements for

00:14:06.875 --> 00:14:10.700
titles and images, and rules for product detail pages.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:17.557
In addition to the product detail page, which all sellers share, your individual offer can impact

00:14:17.557 --> 00:14:19.700
a customer's decision to buy.

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:23.300
An important part of any offer is price.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:28.700
All sellers' prices have to comply with Amazon's Marketplace Fair Pricing Policy.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:34.907
Before you start setting prices in Seller Central, you'll want to get familiar with a few key concepts

00:14:34.907 --> 00:14:38.700
we use to organize and support pricing in the Amazon Store.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:42.700
The first concept is a competitive external price.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:49.700
By that, we mean the lowest price for an item from major retailers outside Amazon.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:55.700
Amazon regularly monitors and shares competitive external prices with sellers as a point of reference.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:15:02.281
For your own price to be considered competitive in the Amazon Store, your standard item price plus

00:15:02.281 --> 00:15:07.700
shipping must be less than or equal to the competitive external price we share.

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:14.759
Competitive external prices also inform another key concept we use to organize offers within the

00:15:14.759 --> 00:15:15.700
Amazon Store.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.800
The Featured Offer.

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:23.767
A product's featured offer is the offer a customer often sees near the top of a product detail page

00:15:23.767 --> 00:15:26.700
with Buy Now and Add to Cart buttons.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:30.700
To compete for the featured offer, a seller must set a competitive price.

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:36.700
Their product also needs to be in new condition and they need to have a professional selling account.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:43.805
Importantly, a seller may also become ineligible for the featured offer based on account performance

00:15:43.805 --> 00:15:45.700
and other risk factors.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:51.700
This helps Amazon guard against abuse and ensure that customers have a great shopping experience.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:58.046
In addition to competitive external prices and featured offers, another key pricing concept is the

00:15:58.046 --> 00:16:02.700
lowest price currently offered by a seller in the Amazon Store.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:08.546
We share the current lowest Amazon price for each product with the sellers who list it to give them

00:16:08.546 --> 00:16:10.700
the opportunity to match or beat it.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:17.900
To view the lowest Amazon price for a product you sell, open the Seller Central Main Menu, hover

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:20.700
over Inventory and click Manage All Inventory.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:27.907
You'll see the featured offer for the product too and can click View More to see the featured offer,

00:16:27.907 --> 00:16:31.700
Competitive External Price and Lowest Amazon Price Side-by-Side.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:37.700
After you list and price a product, the next step is fulfillment or delivery to your customers.

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.700
Amazon sellers can fulfill orders in two ways.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:46.700
One way is to ship products directly to customers, which we call seller or merchant fulfillment.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:50.700
For short, this method is also called MFN.

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:57.288
Sellers can also send products to Amazon for fulfillment, which we call fulfillment by Amazon or

00:16:57.288 --> 00:16:57.700
FBA.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:03.700
The products you send to Amazon are stored in our network of fulfillment centers.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:08.700
When a customer places an order, we pick, pack and ship it on your behalf.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.700
We also take care of customer service.

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:16.700
You can fulfill all your orders as MFN or with FBA exclusively.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:23.700
You can also use each method on a per-product basis to take advantage of their different benefits.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:29.700
Let's review a few key aspects of each fulfillment method starting with MFN.

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:33.700
Fulfilling orders yourself puts you in control of the customer experience.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:39.700
It also means you're responsible for prepping, packing and arranging transit and delivery for orders.

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:44.700
You'll handle customer service too, including returns and refunds.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:50.961
If you're fulfilling as an MFN seller, one of the first places in Seller Central you should visit

00:17:50.961 --> 00:17:52.700
is the Shipping Settings page.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:58.700
Hover over the gear icon to open the Account Settings menu, then click Shipping Settings.

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:04.700
The Shipping Settings page shows your shipping rates and restrictions for seller-fulfilled orders,

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:08.700
which include your geographic shipping regions and service levels.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:12.700
Your account has default shipping settings when it's first created,

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:18.613
but you can use templates to customize them, adjusting the regions you ship to, and the service

00:18:18.613 --> 00:18:20.700
levels you support for each region.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:24.700
You can also use shipping settings to adjust how you calculate shipping fees.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:29.700
Choose between a per item, per pound rate, or price band rate.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:35.700
If you adjust shipping settings, remember that standard shipping is a requirement for all sellers.

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:42.288
Before selecting any additional service levels, you should also confirm that you can meet the indicated

00:18:42.288 --> 00:18:42.700
commitment.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:46.700
MFN sellers manage their own returns and refunds too.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:53.825
Click Return Settings in the Settings menu, then use the four tabs at the top to review and update

00:18:53.825 --> 00:18:55.700
return settings for your business.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:19:01.700
As an MFN seller, you can set specific terms for your own refund and return policies.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:06.700
However, those terms must meet or exceed Amazon's return policy.

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:13.900
When Amazon receives a return request from a customer that meets the terms of our policy, we authorize

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:14.700
it automatically.

00:19:14.700 --> 00:19:21.700
When a return request isn't covered by our return policy, we notify MFN sellers by email.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:28.309
You can then hover over Orders in the main menu and click Manage Returns to authorize or close the

00:19:28.309 --> 00:19:29.700
return or refund request.

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:34.700
You'll do so by deciding whether it meets the specific terms of your policy.

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:39.700
If you close a request, we recommend contacting the customer to explain your decision.

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:45.700
We provide sellers with access to our buyer-seller messaging service for this purpose.

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:50.700
You can access this service by clicking the envelope icon in Seller Central.

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:56.700
Buyer-seller messaging is the only approved method for communicating with Amazon customers.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:02.700
Follow our communication guidelines to help keep your messages compliant and customer-centric.

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:08.613
When you receive an order from a customer that you're fulfilling directly, you need to confirm that

00:20:08.613 --> 00:20:10.700
it's been shipped in Seller Central.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:17.540
Hover over Orders in the main menu, then click Manage Orders to see a list of your orders, view

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:19.700
order details, and print packing slips.

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:24.700
You can use three metrics to help assess the health of your MFN shipping performance.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:32.830
Late shipment rate or LSR, pre-fulfillment cancel rate, also known as the cancellation rate or CR,

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:35.700
and valid tracking rate or VTR.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:42.700
Hover over Performance in the main menu, then click Account Health to view all three metrics.

00:20:42.700 --> 00:20:49.100
Your LSR is the percentage of your seller-fulfilled orders that have a shipping confirmation after

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.700
their expected shipping date.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:55.144
We calculate LSR in both 10 and 30-day periods.

00:20:55.144 --> 00:20:58.700
You should aim to keep it below 4%.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:03.700
Your CR is the percentage of your seller-fulfilled orders you cancel.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:06.967
We calculate CR in 7-day periods.

00:21:06.967 --> 00:21:10.700
You should aim to keep it below 2.5%.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:17.700
Your VTR is the percentage of packages from your seller-fulfilled orders with a valid tracking number.

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:21.433
We calculate VTR in 30-day periods.

00:21:21.433 --> 00:21:25.700
You should aim to keep it above 95%.

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:32.811
You can also use the Account Health Dashboard to monitor your customer service performance and Amazon

00:21:32.811 --> 00:21:33.700
policy compliance.

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:36.700
We'll touch on both later in this video.

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:42.795
If, instead of managing fulfillment yourself, you'd like Amazon to take care of packing and shipping

00:21:42.795 --> 00:21:44.700
orders, you can use FBA.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:49.700
With FBA, we also take care of customer service, including returns.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:54.700
FBA sellers can use return settings to set preferences for their returns.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:22:02.492
Your FBA products are eligible for Amazon Prime free two-day shipping, and you can choose optional

00:22:02.492 --> 00:22:05.700
services like product prep, labeling, and repackaging.

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:10.700
To use FBA, you'll first register your selling account for the program.

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:14.700
Then you'll select FBA as your fulfillment method while listing.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:18.700
You can also convert MFN products that you've already listed.

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:21.700
Next, you'll send your products to Amazon.

00:22:21.700 --> 00:22:26.570
After they're received into our fulfillment network, your products are made available to customers,

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:29.700
and we take care of delivery when they're purchased.

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:35.700
You'll use the Send to Amazon workflow each time you send inventory into our fulfillment network.

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:40.700
In Seller Central, hover over Inventory in the main menu.

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:44.700
Then under Fulfillment by Amazon, FBA, click Shipments.

00:22:44.700 --> 00:22:51.332
Next, hover over the Shipments drop-down menu, and click Send to Amazon to start the shipment creation

00:22:51.332 --> 00:22:51.700
process.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:58.557
If you have any questions while using the Send to Amazon workflow, click Learn More or Watch Tutorial

00:22:58.557 --> 00:22:59.700
within each step.

00:22:59.700 --> 00:23:06.100
Now that you know the basics of account setup, listing, and fulfillment, let's review Account Health,

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:09.700
which is an important topic for every Amazon seller.

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:16.700
To sell in the Amazon store, you're required to comply with all applicable laws and Amazon policies.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:23.759
Our Account Health dashboard provides an overview of your account's' adherence to policies and various

00:23:23.759 --> 00:23:24.700
performance targets.

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:30.700
We regularly review the performance of all sellers and notify them when they're off target.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:36.700
But we recommend you actively monitor your account health to help ensure ongoing compliance.

00:23:36.700 --> 00:23:43.311
Hover over Performance in the main menu in Seller Central, then click Account Health to view the

00:23:43.311 --> 00:23:43.700
dashboard.

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:49.595
We already reviewed the Shipping Performance section of the Account Health dashboard while learning

00:23:49.595 --> 00:23:51.700
about Seller Fulfillment or MFN.

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:57.700
But let's quickly review the Customer Service Performance and Policy Compliance sections.

00:23:57.700 --> 00:24:04.700
Your Customer Service Performance is measured using what we call an Order Defect Rate or ODR.

00:24:04.700 --> 00:24:10.700
Your ODR is the percentage of your orders with one or more indicators of poor customer service.

00:24:10.700 --> 00:24:17.771
That could be negative customer feedback, which is defined as a one or two-star rating, an approved

00:24:17.771 --> 00:24:21.700
A to Z guarantee claim, or a credit card chargeback.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:30.033
We calculate ODR in 60-day periods and require sellers to maintain an ODR under 1% in order to sell

00:24:30.033 --> 00:24:31.700
in the Amazon store.

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:38.437
The last section of your Account Health dashboard provides an overview of your compliance with key

00:24:38.437 --> 00:24:39.700
Amazon selling policies.

00:24:39.700 --> 00:24:46.700
These include our Intellectual Property, Authenticity, Listing and Restricted Product Policies.

00:24:46.700 --> 00:24:51.700
At the top of the Policy Compliance section, you'll see a rating for your selling account.

00:24:51.700 --> 00:24:58.700
To maintain a good rating, make sure to address any policy violations listed below in a timely manner.

00:24:58.700 --> 00:25:05.700
Note that if your rating is at risk or critical, your account may be at risk of deactivation.

00:25:05.700 --> 00:25:11.700
Click any of the policies listed for more information and to respond to a violation.

00:25:11.700 --> 00:25:17.820
Once you've started selling in the Amazon store, you may want to promote or advertise your products

00:25:17.820 --> 00:25:20.700
or brand to help them reach more customers.

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:26.961
We provide a range of tools and programs which you can explore by hovering over advertising in the

00:25:26.961 --> 00:25:28.700
main menu in Seller Central.

00:25:28.700 --> 00:25:34.882
If you're a professional seller, click Deals to create a lightning or seven-day deal that appears

00:25:34.882 --> 00:25:36.700
on the Amazon Deals page.

00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:44.200
Or click Coupons to create a promotion that customers can see on the Amazon Coupons page in search

00:25:44.200 --> 00:25:46.700
results and on product detail pages.

00:25:46.700 --> 00:25:53.379
Professional sellers with a brand enrolled in brand registry can also use Amazon Vine to put free

00:25:53.379 --> 00:25:57.700
units of their products in the hands of Amazon Invited reviewers.

00:25:57.700 --> 00:26:05.200
These reviewers, or Vine Voices, post insightful opinions about your products which can help other

00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:07.700
customers make informed purchasing decisions.

00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:15.526
To use one or more of our pay-per-click advertising options as a professional seller, click Campaign

00:26:15.526 --> 00:26:17.700
Manager in the Advertising Submenu.

00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:26.060
That will take you to a page where you can start creating three types of Amazon Ads campaigns, sponsored

00:26:26.060 --> 00:26:28.700
products, sponsored brands, and sponsored display.

00:26:28.700 --> 00:26:35.474
Sponsored products ads feature a single product and appear in, alongside, and above customer search

00:26:35.474 --> 00:26:35.926
results.

00:26:35.926 --> 00:26:42.700
Sponsored brands ads are available to professional sellers with a brand enrolled in brand registry.

00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:47.700
They can feature up to three products as well as a logo and headline.

00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:54.311
Or you can create a sponsored brands campaign with an auto-playing video that features a single

00:26:54.311 --> 00:26:54.700
product.

00:26:54.700 --> 00:27:00.700
Sponsored brands ads appear prominently above, alongside, and below search results.

00:27:00.700 --> 00:27:07.238
Sponsored display ads feature a single product and can appear both in and beyond the Amazon Store

00:27:07.238 --> 00:27:10.700
after a customer has viewed a product detail page.

00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:15.700
Or if their other browsing behaviors show they're interested in a product.

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:22.311
Each sponsored campaign type comes with options that can help position your ads in front of relevant

00:27:22.311 --> 00:27:22.700
customers.

00:27:22.700 --> 00:27:28.700
You also control your total budget and only pay when a customer actually clicks an ad.

00:27:28.700 --> 00:27:32.700
You set a bid to choose the maximum amount you'd like to spend per click.

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:39.288
Let's finish our overview of selling in the Amazon Store by learning about customer reviews and

00:27:39.288 --> 00:27:39.700
feedback.

00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:50.609
After a customer buys a product, they can leave a public product review, seller feedback rating,

00:27:50.609 --> 00:27:54.700
or both in the Amazon Store.

00:27:54.700 --> 00:27:56.575
Product reviews describe the quality of a product or its function, while seller feedback ratings

00:27:56.575 --> 00:27:57.700
reflect a customer's overall experience buying from a seller.

00:27:57.700 --> 00:28:03.795
Both types of feedback play an important role in the Amazon shopping experience because they can

00:28:03.795 --> 00:28:05.700
be reviewed by other customers.

00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:11.700
Here are some quick tips to improve your chances of getting positive reviews and ratings.

00:28:11.700 --> 00:28:12.200
1.

00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:16.700
Accurately represent a product on your product detail page.

00:28:16.700 --> 00:28:17.200
2.

00:28:17.200 --> 00:28:21.700
Package your products to help prevent damage during delivery.

00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:22.100
3.

00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:25.700
Ship orders on time if you're an MFN seller.

00:28:25.700 --> 00:28:26.233
4.

00:28:26.233 --> 00:28:33.700
Monitor your inventory quantity so that customers can't accidentally purchase out of stock items.

00:28:33.700 --> 00:28:34.200
5.

00:28:34.200 --> 00:28:39.700
Provide customer refunds for products returned within 30 days of purchase.

00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:40.200
6.

00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:43.700
Respond to customer messages within 24 hours.

00:28:43.700 --> 00:28:44.155
7.

00:28:44.155 --> 00:28:48.700
Provide valid tracking numbers so customers can track their orders.

00:28:48.700 --> 00:28:54.700
To manage and track customer feedback, use our feedback manager in Seller Central.

00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:58.700
Hover over Performance, then click Feedback in the main menu.

00:28:58.700 --> 00:29:03.700
You can review your feedback rating and see recent customer comments.

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:11.004
To post a public reply to a comment or request its removal, use the drop-down menu at the end of

00:29:11.004 --> 00:29:11.700
a row.

00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:15.700
This concludes our 30-minute overview of selling in the Amazon Store.

00:29:15.700 --> 00:29:22.700
We encourage you to explore additional trainings in Seller University about each topic we covered.

00:29:22.700 --> 00:29:26.700
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon Store!
